XB-Kidux-Name-en: Kydux
XB-Kidux-Description-en: A game of the Kidux family for learning to program in Python: a young wizard arrives at a school of magic, and every step there is taken by writing Python code. A fun story, short lessons and levels solved with a small program, with help so as not to get stuck. Free, in English and Spanish, with no account. Requires internet.
XB-Kidux-Name-es: Kydux
XB-Kidux-Description-es: Un juego de la familia Kidux para aprender a programar en Python: un mago o maga llega a un colegio de magia, y allí cada paso se da escribiendo código Python. Una historia divertida, lecciones cortas y niveles que se resuelven con un pequeño programa, con ayudas para no atrancarse. Gratis, en español y en inglés, sin cuenta. Requiere conexión a internet.
XB-Kidux-Ages: 8-
Description: Kidux learning module: Kydux, a door to the family's game for learning Python
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This learning
 module opens Kydux, a game of the Kidux family in which a child learns
 real Python at a school of magic, in a window of its own, and no other
 website: a link to anywhere else leads nowhere. Nothing of the game is
 in this package; it is played on its site, kydux.kidux.org, where anyone
 plays it in a web browser, without Kidux.
 .
 It needs the internet whenever it is used. It is free, in English and
 Spanish, and asks for no account. The game asks whether it may use
 cookies to count how it is played.
 .
 Once it is installed, an adult switches it on for each child on the
 Modules page of the adult panel.
